From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:54:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs101-raven: add the rear flash
 LED

The Pixel 6 Pro's rear flash LED driver is a TI LM3644 at 0x63 on I2C 7
(USI7), with its HWEN on gpp23-6, as stock's raven device tree describes
it. Torch only, capped at 50 mA per channel (a bring-up limit).

Tested on raven (7.3.0-rc6): the driver reads the LM3644TT (device ID
0x04) and offers 17 torch steps, 2550-49110 uA per channel; the LED
turns on and off by hand and from the shell's torch tile (brightnessctl
through logind, no udev rule needed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-raven.dts    | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-raven.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-raven.dts
index 1f4f95779..d48e0ae97 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-raven.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-raven.dts
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 /dts-v1/;
 
+#include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 #include "gs101-pixel-common.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -297,3 +298,32 @@ &pmic {
 	/* for the charger cell */
 	monitored-battery = <&battery>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Rear flash LED: TI LM3644 at 0x63 on PERIC0 USI7 (Google's I2C bus 7, also
+ * the cameras' bus), HWEN on gpp23-6, as stock's raven device tree
+ * describes it. Stock drives it from the camera HAL through LWIS; torch only
+ * here, with cheetah's bring-up cap (not a stock value).
+ */
+&usi7 {
+	samsung,mode = <USI_MODE_I2C>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&hsi2c_7 {
+	clock-frequency = <370000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	led-controller@63 {
+		compatible = "ti,lm3644";
+		reg = <0x63>;
+		enable-gpios = <&gpp23 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+		led {
+			function = LED_FUNCTION_TORCH;
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
+			led-sources = <1 2>;
+			led-max-microamp = <50000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
